 ## Overview
-Sparse Marching Cubes generates a triangle mesh from a sparse set of 3D points with associated scalar values (e.g., Signed Distance Fields), avoiding the memory overhead of dense 3D grids [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard Marching Cubes by dynamically gathering corner values for active voxels via lookup, rather than iterating over a fixed dense volume [S1, unofficial].
+Sparse Marching Cubes generates a triangle mesh from a sparse set of 3D points with scalar values (e.g., Signed Distance Fields), avoiding the memory overhead of dense 3D grids [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard Marching Cubes by dynamically gathering corner values for active voxels via lookup, rather than iterating over a fixed dense volume [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Marching Cubes Lookup and Configuration](2518-marching-cubes-lookup-and-configuration.md) by applying its topology logic only to voxels explicitly defined in the input point cloud.
 
